 s Peoples Day Powwow & Indian Market 534 Years of Resistance & Renewal Ber
 keley’s Indigenous Peoples Day Committee invites the public to celebrate
  the 34th Annual Indigenous Peoples Day Powwow & Indian Market on Saturday
 \, October 10\, 2026\, at M.L.K. Civic Center Park from 10:00 am to 6:00 p
 m. This free\, family-friendly celebration will bring together Native Amer
 ican dancers\, drummers\, artists\, craftspeople\, food vendors\, and comm
 unity members for a day of culture\, ceremony\, celebration\, and communit
 y. The Powwow will feature powwow dancing and drumming\, along with compet
 ition dancing. There will also be Gourd dancing and songs\, dance specials
 \, Intertribals and Round Dances that everyone is invited to join. Childre
 n are welcome. What: Berkeley’s 34th Annual Indigenous Peoples Day Powwo
 w & Indian Market When: Saturday\, October 10\, 2026 10 a.m.– 6 p.m. Gra
 nd Entry: 1 p.m. Where: M.L.K. Civic Center Park Allston Way at M.L. King\
 , Jr. Way Berkeley\, California Head Staff Co-MCs: Randy Pico (Luiseño) &
